<title>USA: US soy crush highest in two years--Census Bureau.</title>
<headline>US soy crush highest in two years--Census Bureau.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean crush for the past two months has run at the highest levels in recent years, a Census Bureau official said Thursday.</p>
<p>Crush in January was 137.265 million bushels, or 4,117,962 short tons, down slightly from December's 138.218 million bushels, or 4,146,540 tons, Census said in a monthly report issued earlier in the day.</p>
<p>Traders had anticipated record-level crush in January as a reflection of strong export demand for soybeans and products.</p>
<p>A Census Bureau official said December and January crush was the highest in two years and was a &quot;very substantial&quot; level.  </p>
<p>Here are Census figures on soy crush during 1996 (million bu):</p>
<p>--December, 138.218</p>
<p>--November, 133.105.</p>
<p>--October, 129.992.</p>
<p>--September, 100,540.</p>
<p>--August, 105.571.</p>
<p>--July, 111.906.</p>
<p>--June, 107.459.</p>
<p>--May, 106.331.</p>
<p>--April, 112.140.</p>
<p>--March, 115.492.</p>
<p>--February, 111.196.</p>
<p>--January, 122.803.</p>
